From bc9688f69ff64af1737168ee158fc3082854869c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:08:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VR battle table, VR guide and the VR battle map / guide
 options

In VR with "VR battle map" Battle table (default) the tactical map hovers flat
in front of the player as a holographic table (after BattleGroupVR): the
game picture reprojected from its camera onto a horizontal table, unit icons
on stalks, the full picture on a screen beyond, translucent glove hands, a
drag beam for orders, haptic pulses (an OpenXR vibration action, suggested
with a fallback), table turn by twisting both grips. ga2_battletable carries
the state between the game side (native/compat/ga2_battlepointer.cpp) and
ga2_vr. ga2_vr_input: Scene::TacticalTable (press-drag-release Circle,
grips belong to the table). ga2_vrguide: an interactive guide to the VR
controls (basics at the screen, the battle part at the table, a card that
translates the game tutorial's gated buttons into VR gestures), option
"VR guide" (show / battle / basics / done), replay by the table's ?.
Unit tests for the input scene and the guide.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
